✅ Git Learning Schedule (7 Days Plan)

Goal: Learn Git step-by-step for real-world DevOps usage and interview preparation
**********************************************************************************


---

# Day 1.  – Git Basics & Setup

What is Git?

Git vs GitHub

Install Git and create a GitHub account

Configure Git (git config --global)

Create a local repo (git init)

Stage → Commit process

Commands: git add, git commit -m

Check status: git status, git log
🔁 Practice: Create a folder, add files, track and commit changes




---

# Day 2 – Tracking File Changes

See file changes using git diff

Delete and rename files

Commands: git rm, git mv


Show file history: git show

Restore files: git checkout filename

Use .gitignore to skip files
🔁 Practice: Try adding/removing files and ignore some files



---

# Day 3 – Branching

What is a branch?

Create, switch, and delete branches

Commands: git branch, git switch, git checkout


Merging branches

Understand and resolve merge conflicts
🔁 Practice: Create a branch, make changes, merge it into main branch



---

# Day 4 – Remote Repositories & GitHub

What is a remote repo?

Create a GitHub repo

Link local repo to GitHub

Commands: git remote add origin, git push -u origin main


Clone a repo: git clone

Pull updates: git pull
🔁 Practice: Push local code to GitHub and pull it on another folder/machine



---

# Day 5 – Stashing, Tagging, Reset & Revert

Save temporary work: git stash, git stash apply

Tag versions: git tag, git show <tag>

Undo changes using:

git reset (soft/hard)

git revert (safe undo)
🔁 Practice: Make and stash changes, create tags, try revert/reset




---

# Day 6 – Real-World Git Workflow

Git Workflow (Feature, Dev, Main branches)

Fork and Pull Request (PR)

Code collaboration

Solve real merge conflicts
🔁 Practice: Collaborate with a friend on GitHub using PR



---

# Day 7 – Advanced Concepts & Interview Prep

Reflog and recovering lost commits

Cherry-pick

Squash commits

Git best practices

Important Git interview questions
🔁 Practice: Try reflog, cherry-pick, and revise all commands